  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/comments/551967103",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/112#issuecomment-551967103",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/112",
    "id": 551967103,
    "node_id": "MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU1MTk2NzEwMw==",
    "user": {
      "login": "hiroshige-g",
      "id": 11661256,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjExNjYxMjU2",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11661256?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/hiroshige-g",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2019-11-08T19:51:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-11-08T19:51:05Z",
    "body": "> (just like module scripts have stricter MIME type restriction than classic scripts)\r\n\r\nIIUC:\r\nClassic scripts allow MIME sniffing and accept a quite broad range of MIME types, including `text/html` which are clearly non-JavaScript, can be executed as scripts by attacks/mistake but are widely used.\r\nModule scripts are new and don't have to be worried about breaking existing scripts, so allow only strict JavaScript MIME types for improved security.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure whether similar argument applies to JSON modules.\r\n\r\nThe benefit to allow `*/*+json` would be clarifying that we allow a broad range of MIME types (including e.g. `image/foobar+json`) intentionally as JSON modules.\r\n\r\nThe benefit to narrow the range would be improving security. https://github.com/w3c/webcomponents/issues/839 will make JSON modules NOT to SOLELY rely on MIME types, but will we still need MIME type checks as a part of security guard? I don't have specific concerning cases for now and thus I filed this issue whether someone has specific thoughts aboud security.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/comments/551967103/reactions",
