    "body": "Ah, that's what you meant. So yes, requiring a JSON MIME type is important, just like it's important to require a JavaScript MIME type in new contexts (especially if they can parse differently), but it doesn't have to be a specific one, as far as I can tell.\r\n\r\nNavigation is observable if you navigate an `<iframe>` or popup to a JSON response. Per those rules it ought to be rendered (and be accessible) as a text document.",
