    "created_at": "2019-11-11T17:01:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-11-11T17:01:44Z",
    "body": "> Is anyone familiar with the reasoning behind that decision? That could help inform our thinking here. In particular I wonder if it was just a simplification or if there was some security concern.\r\n\r\nIt is a security concern. There have been attacks in the past (e.g. [this paper](https://www.mbsd.jp/Whitepaper/xssi.pdf) (C)) based on non-JS files being treated as JS files and \"executed\".\r\n\r\nIn general, allowing web sites to treat the contents of URLs as a different type than their declared content-type is an attack vector that gets exploited fairly regularly.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
