    "created_at": "2019-11-13T20:03:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-11-13T20:03:51Z",
    "body": "I'm thinking that in this case the benefit of allowing potential JSON-like types like `image/foobar+json` to be loaded as JSON modules outweighs any benefit of narrowing the JSON MIME-type set.  I understand now the security concerns of loading non-JS as script, but it's hard to see how parsing even arbitrary content as JSON could be harmful on the same level.  And adding `+json` to a MIME type seems like a pretty straightforward signal that the resource owner expects that it could be interpreted as JSON.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/comments/553577943/reactions",
      "total_count": 2,
      "+1": 2,
      "-1": 0,
