    "minimized": null
  },
  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/comments/555201801",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/112#issuecomment-555201801",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/112",
    "id": 555201801,
    "node_id": "MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU1NTIwMTgwMQ==",
    "user": {
      "login": "hiroshige-g",
      "id": 11661256,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjExNjYxMjU2",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11661256?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/hiroshige-g",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hiroshige-g/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2019-11-18T20:47:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-11-18T20:47:15Z",
    "body": "So, the concensus here can be:\r\n- Importing `*/*+json`, including `image/foobar+json` has valid use cases\r\n- Importing (and navigating to) `*/*+json` doesn't look to cause security problems (because JSON isn't executed)\r\n- so let's keep the current spec and allow `*/*+json` as-is.\r\n\r\nDoes this sounds good?\r\n\r\nIf so, Chromium will allow `*/*+json` for JSON modules.\r\nIf fixing the existing interoperability issue of navigation + `*/*+json` is desired, we might want to file a Pri-3 bug against Chromium (and other browsers), but currently I don't have immediate motivation to changing Chromium's behavior around navigation.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
